    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n5 Woodpark is a well located five bedroom semi-detached home, conveniently situated in a quiet residential cul de sac, midway between Westport town centre and The Quay.\n\nThe house was built circa 1994, and a two storey extension was added to the side in 2006 to provide a substantial residence. A new owner may wish to carry out some modernisation and redecoration work. The property would make a superb family home within easy reach of Westport's amenities, an investment with good income potential or and ideally placed holiday home in one the West of Ireland's most popular destinations. \n\nThe well proportioned floor area measures approximately 138.6 sq m (1,492 sq ft). The ground floor accommodation comprises of entrance hall with guest WC, a south facing living room, a large kitchen/dining room with an adjoining utility room, and a large en-suite double bedroom which is currently utilised as a sitting room. \n\nOn the first floor there are four bedrooms (two with en-suite shower rooms), three double rooms and one single, and a main bathroom. \n\nTo the rear is a courtyard style garden with side access and a block shed (2.8m x 2.45m) with electricity. The front garden has off street parking for a number of cars. \n\nWoodpark is a mature residential cul de sac of 12 houses which is a short walk from Westport Quay where there is a good range of facilities including National School, small supermarket, shops and award winning restaurants and bars. \n\nWestport town centre and its many amenities are 1.2 kilometre from the property and can be accessed via the nearby Westport Greenway, a 2.6 km walking/cycle path linking Westport town and Quay.\n\n OFFERS IN EXCESS OF 459,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch - 1.67m x 0.65m\nTiled floor\n\nEntrance Hall - 4.86m x 1.88m\nOak floor, carpeted stairs\n\nLiving Room - 4.48m x 3.88m\nOak floor, timber and marble fireplace with inset solid fuel stove\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 3.88m x 3.56m & 2.45m x 1.01m\nTiled floor, oak style kitchen with granite counter tops, built in dresser unit\n\nUtility Room - 4.0m x 2.26m\nTiled floor, built in floor and wall units with sink, door to rear garden\n\nBedroom One - 4.78m x 2.78m\nCurrently used as a sitting room, oak floor\n\nEn-Suite - 2.55nm x 0.92m\nTiled floor, part tiled walls, shower, wc, whb\n\nWC - \nTiled floor, wc, whb\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 2.92m x 1.05m & 0.86m x 0.8m\nCarpeted\n\nBedroom Two - 3.59m x 3.26m\nCarpeted, built in wardrobes\n\nEn-Suite - 1.51m x 0.87m\nTiled floor and part tiled walls, shower, wc, whb\n\nBedroom Three - 2.6m x 2.48m\nLaminate floor (single room)\n\nBedroom Four - 3.66m x 2.99m\nLaminate floor, built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom Five - 4.72m x 2.78m & 1.09m x 0.91m\nCarpeted, built in storage press\n\nEn-Suite - 2.78m x 1.19m\nTiled floor and part tiled walls, shower, wc, whb, heated towel rail\n\nBathroom - 2.05m x 1.77m\nFully tiled, bath/shower, wc, whb, heated towel rail\n\nHotpress - 1.02m x 0.68m\n\n\n"
      },
